with test master set to step into the  upcoming Black Widow movie it's time to  dive into a long history that's strange  even by the standards of the Marvel  Universe  from a school for supervillains to the  South American village populated by  Hitler clones here's the truth behind  the taskmaster the taskmaster made his  first appearance in 1980s Avengers  number 195 arriving on the last page to  set up his full appearance in the next  issue man kick off a long career of  supervillain exploits created by david  michelinie and Jorge Perez he has a  superpower usually referred to as  photographic reflexes that's a fancy way  of saying that if he sees someone doing  something he can replicate that action  exactly Andy keeps that skill for the  rest of his life that would be a pretty  impressive ability in the real world but  this is a dude who lives in the Marvel  Universe he can settle in with some  footage of spider-man or black panther  and hop off the couch a few hours later  with the ability to perfectly replicate  their movements of course there's a  limit to all this photographic reflexes  are taskmasters only power that means  that while he can watch Captain America  throwing his shield and replicate the  movement it doesn't have caps  super-strength behind it still he's come  away from his many battles against the  Avengers with some pretty impressive  abilities while he's done his share of  hands-on villainy the task masters Tru  Calling has always been in education of  course his school the taskmaster Academy  is less of a learning institution and  more of a for-profit training center for  henchmen for a low price  taskmaster teaches classes of aspiring  supervillains not only how to fight like  superheroes but more importantly how to  fight against them while this mostly  functions as a pretty fantastic  explanation for where all the masked  members of Hydra and aim get the  confidence to try to punch out Iron Man  it's worth noting that it's not just the  bad guys who've taken advantage of the  taskmaster skills  he's also been responsible for training  a few of the good guys as well as the  supervillain mercenary the taskmaster  doesn't have a whole lot of friends but  one of his more enduring acquaintances  came in the form of another mercenary  Deadpool the two characters had a rocky  start to their relationship first  meeting when taskmaster attempted to use  Deadpool as a training dummy for his  students only to be foiled when Deadpool  threw him off by breaking into a  dance-off during their fight it turns  out he can only counter your moves if he  can predict them and as you may already  know Deadpool can be  unpredictable after that one of the  taskmasters most predominant roles in  the comics came when he was a member of  Deadpool supporting cast and in more  recent years the two mercenaries have  had a more back-and-forth frenemy  relationship they've occasionally come  to blows while on opposite sides of a  conflict but Deadpool was always willing  to help taskmaster out by going easy on  him in a fight  so the skull-faced opportunists could  still get paid here's where it gets a  little weird  while he's mostly shown up as a villain  or a supporting character the taskmaster  has dabbled in being a protagonist in  his own right thanks to two self-titled  miniseries the first is a relatively  straightforward action-adventure but  that second story is full on bananas the  main premise is that the taskmaster  ironically enough has a memory problem  his brain is so loaded up with shank  cheese punches and Daredevils backflips  that his muscle memory has overwritten  other plus important things like his  past to solve that he tries to track  down his own memories that leads him  through things like an encounter with  the Dawn of the Dead a Latin American  drug dealer who turns out to be a white  American SHIELD agent who taken the dawn  of the dead identity after taskmaster  trained him that however pales in  comparison to where that series ends up  be Bell's burg to a small town in the  South American Andes where Nazi  scientists escaped after World War 2 to  attempt to clone Hitler the most  successful result was the longtime  Marvel villain the hate monger who first  showed up back in 1963 but the  scientists wound up with a gigantic  stockpile of cloned Hitler brains which  leaked the bureau's biochemical essence  into the local water supply the result  every man woman and child in the town  essentially has Hitler's brain leading  to a constant warfare among themselves  for control of the area so you know the  next time someone tries to tell you how  serious the punisher is or whatever  remind them that he lives in the same  world as Hitler town beyond V bells burg  - in the dawn of the dead.the big  reveals of the taskmaster series are the  title character's origin and real name  for years the taskmaster has been  getting his orders from a secret  organization called the org but as it  turns out the org doesn't actually exist  instead it's the wife that taskmaster  doesn't remember having Mercedes Merced  who was also his partner back when he  was a SHIELD agent named wait for it  Tony masters as Nick Fury tells Steve  Rogers the taskmaster has been a good  all along he just doesn't remember it as  masters he was sent to infiltrate the  supervillain community for shield taking  the taskmaster identity as his cover  unfortunately thanks to a flawed  prototype of the Super Soldier Serum  that expanded his powers all of those  skills he'd absorbed over wrote the  personal parts of his memory  Mercedes has been minimizing the damage  for years by acting as taskmasters  handler and pointing him in the right  directions of course once he discovers  all this his brain immediately erases it  in favor of another new fighting style  putting a heartbroken Mercedes right  back into the role of working with a  husband who doesn't remember she exists  while it's doubtful that say that Dawn  of the Dead will show up it's not  difficult to imagine how taskmaster  might fit into the Black Widow movie  most of Natasha Romanovs history has to  do with her training in the Red Room a  secret Soviet program designed to create  a series of highly trained agents who  were given the codename of Black Widow  with the taskmasters history and his  ability to serve as the perfect teacher  in virtually any style of combat it's  easy to picture him as one of Natasha's  trainers and maybe even the person who's  sent to clean things up once she defects  the shield sure that's a pretty  straightforward espionage plot but it's  also one that could fit neatly into the  world of the MCU then again given that  we've seen Infinity stones the  Celestials and a talking raccoon in  those movies there's always a chance  that taskmaster and Widow will end up  fighting a climactic battle in Beebe  ellsberg to seeing Marvel characters  beating up a couple hundred Hitler's  might just make Black Widow the  feel-good movie of the year check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite stuff are coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

